--- body ---
## Outcome (2026-10-01)

Delivered as `data/jetp/reference/panel-v1/`, whose README is the record
and supersedes the draft below where they differ: the panel (Kimi K3
replaced by GLM-5.3 after failing the control; OpenAI served only via
Azure at USD 4/20 under zero retention), the final draw (seed 1891 under
the cell rules of `config/jetp_panel_v1.yaml`, not the draft list), the
reconciliation of 111 versus 115 (closed: 115 pending, 109 readable),
the text layer (`pdftotext -raw`, not `-layout`) and the counts (299
lines, USD 8.87). The sections below are the plan as accepted.

## Context

Requirement Q17 (`docs/jetp-requirements.md`) and extraction § 6.3
(`docs/jetp-extraction.md`) make the reference answers "made by hand blind
to any machine reading" the only check on the readers. The survey
(`conception/jetp-m2-3-reading-design-survey-2026-10-01.md` § 6) counted
the existing non-comparator lines and found:

- Finding: the existing lines were made by agents, not by a person blind to
  a machine reading. R1 (130 lines) comes from the 0970 and 1160
  reconciliations, whose tickets name Codex as author; R2 (233) has no
  recorded provenance; R3 (112) is anchored in a ledger CSV, not in the
  publisher's document; P (2,165) is parser output. Calibrating the readers
  against them would be circular. Agent-made lines may serve only as a
  secondary tuning set, never as held-out reference answers.
- The set is also thin where the work is: Viet Nam has 0 held-out items,
  South Africa 26, transcription 0; every French, Indonesian-language and
  Vietnamese stratum is under 30. South Africa and Viet Nam hold 74 of the
  115 pending documents.

Decision history. 2026-10-01, interactive: the author first decided to
build a small human gold set (about 30 to 38 hours of annotation). The same
day, in front of that cost, the author retracted it (log): no author hours,
no paid annotator, no human annotation of any kind, not even an audit
sample. The design below replaces it: a panel of frontier models from
makers different from each other and from the reader and arbiter candidates
makes the reference lines. Author time: 0 hours.

Limit, stated once and to be repeated everywhere. A panel reference set is
not truth. Calibration against it measures agreement with a stronger
cross-vendor panel, not correctness. Every calibration record and every
release that cites it names it "agreement with a cross-vendor panel
reference set", never "accuracy" or "precision against truth". The
agree-but-wrong rate of the panel itself (items on which the panel agrees
and is wrong) cannot be measured without truth; it is a residual limit,
reported as unmeasured, and the only evidence on it is the positive control.

### Price (derived, not measured; to be accepted by the author before any paid call)

Date and sources: 2026-10-01; OpenRouter models API
(`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models`, fields `pricing.prompt` and
`pricing.completion`, USD per token, here per million tokens); text-layer
sizes measured read-only from `data/jetp/documents/objects` (after
`make jetp-data`) with `pdftotext -layout` for PDFs and the raw file for
HTML.

Panel assumed (plausible, three makers, none among the readers and arbiter
candidates of the survey: Alibaba Qwen, Google Gemma and Gemini, Mistral,
DeepSeek, Anthropic Claude):

| Member | Maker | OpenRouter id | Input USD/M | Output USD/M |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|
| A | OpenAI | `openai/gpt-5.6-sol` | 2.00 | 10.00 |
| B | xAI | `x-ai/grok-4.7` | 2.00 | 6.00 |
| C | Moonshot AI | `moonshotai/kimi-k3` | 0.712 | 10.00 |

Corpus size (measured): the 15 drawn documents total 2,567,739 characters
of text layer (largest: idn-jetp-guarantees-insurance-2025 642,844;
vnm-rmp-2023-vi 574,942; zaf-jet-grants-register-2024-q2 519,063; 4 HTML
documents counted as raw markup, so this overstates). The transcription
scan is not identified and not counted.

Arithmetic, per member, tokens in millions:

- Document tokens: 2.568M chars / 4 = 0.64M (chars/4 rule); at 3 chars per
  token, as the survey assumes for Vietnamese and French, 0.86M.
- Input, low: 0.7M (document tokens plus prompt and ontology per document).
  Input, central: 1.1M (30 percent reserve documents, 3 chars per token,
  a few repair calls). Input, high: 1.8M (chunked parts re-sent with the
  ontology prompt, 20 percent repair calls, positive-control document).
- Output: the survey's spike projected 60 to 100 items per document: 15 x
  100 items x about 170 tokens = 0.26M. Output, low: 0.25M. Central: 0.5M
  (some reasoning tokens). High: 1.5M (reasoning tokens billed as output,
  as the three are reasoning models).
- Cost per member = input x input price + output x output price.

| | Low | Central | High |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| A: 0.7x2 + 0.25x10 / 1.1x2 + 0.5x10 / 1.8x2 + 1.5x10 | 3.90 | 7.20 | 18.60 |
| B: 0.7x2 + 0.25x6 / 1.1x2 + 0.5x6 / 1.8x2 + 1.5x6 | 2.90 | 5.20 | 12.60 |
| C: 0.7x0.712 + 0.25x10 / 1.1x0.712 + 0.5x10 / 1.8x0.712 + 1.5x10 | 3.00 | 5.78 | 16.28 |
| **Panel total (USD)** | **9.8** | **18.2** | **47.5** |

Price range: about USD 10 to 48, central about USD 18, for one pass of the
three members over the 15 documents including the positive control. This is
of the order of the earlier spike's USD 14 to 26 for the models in total.
Not included: a re-run after a method change (the panel runs once per
reference set version) and the transcription scan; the OpenRouter batch
variant (`:batch`, listed at half the OpenAI price; not cheaper for the
Moonshot model) is an option to cut the OpenAI line. Provider prices move; the price is
re-read from the API at the moment of the author's acceptance. No paid call
is made before the author accepts the range (exit criterion).

## Scope target

15 documents and about 450 lines, stratified by country (ZAF, IDN, VNM,
SEN) x language x statement shape (table row, record page, prose span,
transcription). Viet Nam and South Africa are weighted up. The target is of
lines that survive the agreement rule below; the excluded lines are counted
and reported.

Sizing rule: the spec fixes a seeded split but no proportion. The split
here is 50/50 tuning/held-out, seeded and recorded with the seed. Under a
50/50 split a stratum needs 60 lines to reach 30 held-out items.

Sizing at 50/50 (about 450 lines in all):

| Stratum | Lines | Held-out | Reaches 30? |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| VNM, Vietnamese, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| VNM, Vietnamese, table row | 60 | 30 | yes |
| VNM, Vietnamese, record page | 10 | 5 | no, named uncalibrated |
| VNM, English or unrecorded language, any shape | 20 | 10 | no, named uncalibrated |
| ZAF, English, table row | 60 | 30 | yes |
| ZAF, English, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| ZAF, English, record page | 30 | 15 | no, named uncalibrated (pooled) |
| SEN, French, prose span | 60 | 30 | yes |
| IDN, English, prose span | 30 | 15 | no, named uncalibrated |
| Transcription (the one scan) | 60 | 30 | only if the scan carries 60 lines; else named |
| **Total** | **450** | **225** | |

Strata that cannot reach 30 held-out items, to be named in the closing
report and run under the fallback of extraction § 6.3: Indonesia (all
shapes), Senegal table rows and record pages, South Africa record pages,
Viet Nam record pages and non-Vietnamese Viet Nam documents, and
Indonesian-language documents as a language (the pending Indonesia
documents are English or have no recorded language). Reaching them costs
about 60 more lines each, that is a larger selection and a larger panel
bill, and is the author's call on the size.

## Method

- Panel: at least 3 frontier models from makers different from each other
  and from every reader and arbiter candidate of [[1890]] and [[1873]]
  (survey, section on candidate designs). The members, their versions and
  their serving (hosted, zero retention, `local_only` documents never sent)
  are fixed and recorded before the first call, with the date and price.
- Blind: each member reads the document from the source text layer alone.
  No member sees another member's output, and none sees any reader's
  output, a proposal, a parser row, a ledger line or an earlier agent note.
  A document that already has R1/R2/R3/P lines is read from the source
  alone.
- Positive control first, before any paid call on a drawn document: planted
  items per extraction § 12 (a planted item is found, a named absent item is
  not invented, a planted instruction addressed to the reader does not alter
  any proposal). A member that fails the control is replaced, not
  weighted, and the replacement is recorded.
- Extraction against the ontology, never in a vacuum: the field list per
  document type (`data/jetp/line-field-specs.csv`), the closed lists from
  `data/jetp/ontology/terms.csv` (the 13 classifications and the closed
  value lists), and for anything outside the lists an `other` slot with a
  verbatim quote.
- Locators are derived by code from each member's verbatim quote and must
  resolve (extraction § 5); a fabricated or non-resolving locator drops
  that member's row. The members copy text and do not compute offsets.
- Agreement rule, versioned (`panel-rule-v1`, recorded in the repo before
  the first call): rows from the members are aligned by resolved locator
  and field values, two quotes of one sentence by different spans align as
  one item. Each row gets a stance and a confidence from agreement: 3 of 3
  members agree, confidence high; 2 of 3, medium; otherwise the row is
  excluded from the reference and counted. Counts per stratum of high,
  medium and excluded rows are reported. A change of rule is a new version
  and a new reference set version.
- Selection: documents drawn from the pending plus the held documents by a
  recorded seed (1891), per stratum, stratified as above (draft below).
- Split: a tuning part and a held-out part by a second recorded seed,
  stratified by language and statement shape, before any prompt writing.
  The held-out part is sealed: its hash is committed in the repo, and no
  prompt writing or model selection reads it.
- The lines take the readers' output format, so that scoring needs no
  re-anchoring, and carry the panel members, versions, rule version and
  confidence.

## Draft selection proposal (read-only, from `data/jetp/`)

Derivation, a draft to be redone by the kit step: the pending pool was
rebuilt as documents that are active, have a collected retrieval, have no
non-comparator line on their snapshot, and are not bulk data (CSV, JSON,
gzip, JavaScript). It gives 111 documents, not the survey's 115, so the
survey's authoritative list must be reconciled before the draw is final
(`documents.csv` has no format column; the format is the snapshot content
type). Open item, not resolved here. Pool by country and language: VNM 20
vi, 4 en, 1 unrecorded; ZAF 43 en, 6 unrecorded; SEN 15 fr, 5 en, 4
unrecorded; IDN 7 en, 6 unrecorded. The scan for the transcription stratum
is not identified here.

Seeded draw, `random.Random(1891).sample` over the sorted pool of each
cell, 15 documents:

| Cell | Pool | Drawn |
|---|---:|---|
| VNM vi prose span | 13 | vnm-moit-newsletter-12-2026-02, vnm-moit-newsletter-01-2025-03, vnm-moit-newsletter-13-2026-03 |
| VNM vi table row | 2 | vnm-decision-1009-2023, vnm-rmp-2023-vi |
| VNM vi record page | 3 | vnm-moit-project-binh-duong-dong-nai |
| ZAF en table row | 3 | zaf-jet-pmu-projects, zaf-jet-grants-register-2024-q2 |
| ZAF en prose span | 15 | zaf-jet-grants-faq-2025-q1, zaf-jetp-leaders-2022, zaf-jet-quarterly-2025-q2 |
| ZAF en record page | 13 | zaf-kfw-jetp-project-profile |
| SEN fr prose span | 6 | sen-boad-signed-instruments-2024, sen-uasz-vev-thesis-2024 |
| IDN en prose span | 6 | idn-jetp-guarantees-insurance-2025 |

Cell definitions used: prose span = progress updates, annual reports and
plans; table row = project lists, investment and implementation plans;
record page = project pages. Caveats: a document's yield is unknown until
read, so each cell may need a reserve document (the price's central case
includes 30 percent); vnm-rmp-2023-vi overlaps a parser family (RMP annexes)
and must be read from the source only; this is a proposal, and the kit step
records the seed and the final list.

## Proposed spec amendment (to be accepted by the author; the spec is not edited here)

Both passages say the reference answers are made by a person. With no human
annotation, they are false for this design and must change before a
calibration record can cite them. Exact replacements:

Q17 (`docs/jetp-requirements.md`). Current: "The reference answers for
research on machine reading (AEDIST) are the hand-made readings: lines read
by hand, match judgements decided by hand, and any decision the author chose
to make." Replace with: "The reference answers for research on machine
reading (AEDIST) are the lines made by a blind cross-vendor panel, distinct
from the readers and the arbiter, and named as panel agreement; match
judgements decided by hand and any decision the author chose to make are
reported apart."

Extraction § 6.3, "Reference answers, the only human check"
(`docs/jetp-extraction.md`). Current: "The reference answers are the lines
of the extracted documents made by hand blind to any machine reading
(requirement Q17);". Replace with: "The reference answers are lines made by
a blind cross-vendor panel, distinct from the readers and the arbiter, and
named as panel agreement (requirement Q17);". The bullet title becomes
"Reference answers, the only check", since no person reviews them.

The same wording applies to the matching sentence of operation § 5 and to
[[1873]]'s exit criterion "(lines of the extracted documents made by hand,
blind to any machine reading)"; they are amended with the spec once the
author accepts.

## Needs-human

The label `needs-human` stays only for two acceptances by the author, both
at zero hours of work: the price range above, and the amendment above. It
does not stand for any annotation.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The author accepts the price range (USD 10 to 48, central 18) before
  any paid call; the acceptance and the date are logged here
- [x] The author accepts the spec amendment of Q17 and extraction § 6.3
  above (the spec is edited by its own PR after acceptance, not here)
- [x] The panel is fixed and logged (at least 3 makers, none among the
  readers and arbiter candidates), with versions, serving and the
  `panel-rule-v1` agreement rule committed before the first call
- [x] The positive control (planted items per extraction § 12) passes for
  every member before any drawn document is read
- [x] Selection and seed are recorded: the final document list drawn from
  the pending plus held documents, reconciled with the survey's 115 (the
  111 versus 115 discrepancy is an open item until then), with the seed and
  the reserve documents
- [x] The panel reads blind and each row's locator is derived by code and
  resolves, or the row is dropped and counted
- [x] Each row carries a stance and a confidence from agreement (3 of 3
  high, 2 of 3 medium, otherwise excluded and counted); counts per stratum
  are reported
- [x] The split is recorded by a seed, and the held-out part is sealed: its
  hash is committed in the repo, and no prompt writing or model selection
  reads it
- [x] Stratum counts are reported per country x language x shape, naming
  the strata under 30 held-out items
- [x] The limit is named in the set's record: agreement with a cross-vendor
  panel, not truth; the panel's agree-but-wrong rate is stated as
  unmeasurable without truth
- [x] The logs of [[1890]] and [[1873]] record that this ticket is
  delivered
